  "notes": "Source Table 4 (protocol numbering); table_number 2 in this extraction. Doc p.85 is a single full-page raster image with no text layer and no vector rules: grid read visually, rule lines recovered from the raster (200 dpi), marks confirmed by a near-black pixel-count detector. Doc pp.86-87 carry the '*' note, abbreviations (not emitted) and footnotes a-l only (no activity rows). Classification: same columns as Table 1, but the title restricts it to randomized patients who have completed Visit 2 under COVID-19 modifications, i.e. a schedule entered on a condition -> track (see review item D1). Columns 2 (Visit 1) and 3 (Visit 2) are each one grey cell merged vertically over all 25 activity rows, printing rotated pointer text 'Refer to Global Protocol or Country-Specific Amendment for Visit 1/2 Procedures'; per the vertical-merge rule the pointer is emitted on every activity row's cell in its column (not a whole-schedule cross-reference, since it covers only one column each). Pharmacogenetic Consent and Pharmacogenetic Sample each carry one X in a cell merged over columns 4-7 (Visit 3 to Visit 6/ET), source_range '4:7'. Footnote k has no printed marker in the grid (see D2)."
 },
